// `@debug` is a statement-position BLOCK tier: `@debug { … }` stands alone and decorates nothing.
// Annotating a declaration with it is E0054.
//
// This was accepted until the tier attachment model was unified. `ExtTier.sites` was documented as
// the set of declarations a tier attaches to, but an empty set was read as "unrestricted" — so the
// two tiers that attach to NOTHING (`debug`, `json`) were spelled exactly like a tier that attaches
// to everything, and no gate could act on either without breaking the other. Empty now means what
// it says, and the annotation form is checked rather than silently accepted.
// expect: error E0054 at 11:2
// expect: exit 1
@debug
fn f(): int { return 1 }
echo f()
